// Rule: [T1547.005][T1003.001] Medusa - Mimilib LSA Security Package
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1547.005, T1003.001
// Classification: Production candidate
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR /
// Required telemetry: DeviceRegistryEvents
// Purpose: Source-observed registration of the Mimikatz mimilib Security Support Provider for plaintext credential capture.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceRegistryEvents for mimilib lsa security package using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: Detection boundary: a match proves the Registry value contained "mimilib"; it does not prove the DLL loaded, passwords were captured, or Medusa attribution.
// A match does not prove: Detection boundary: a match proves the Registry value contained "mimilib"; it does not prove the DLL loaded, passwords were captured, or Medusa attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Production candidate - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint registry events on Windows
// Evidence: CISA, FBI and HHS report Medusa actors adding mimilib to the LSA
// Security Packages REG_MULTI_SZ value so the credential-stealing SSP loads in LSASS.
// Detection boundary: a match proves the Registry value contained "mimilib"; it does
// not prove the DLL loaded, passwords were captured, or Medusa attribution.
DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith @"\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa"
| where RegistryValueName =~ "Security Packages"
| where RegistryValueData contains "mimilib"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    ReportId,
    ActionType,
    RegistryKey,
    RegistryValueName,
    RegistryValueType,
    RegistryValueData,
    PreviousRegistryValueData,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    InitiatingProcessUniqueId
| order by Timestamp desc
